<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trpimirović dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Trpimirović dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, first as dukes and from about 925 as kings, from the mid-9th century to the late 11th century. Named after Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trpimir-i">Trpimir I</a>, it included Tomislav, the first king, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petar-kresimir-iv">Petar Krešimir IV</a>. The line ended with the death of Stephen II around 1091, and the succession struggle that followed led to the union of Croatia with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1102.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trpimirovic-dynasty.jpg" alt="Trpimirović dynasty" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kresimir%27s_seal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
